---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Writing — HarvTech"
  description="Technical writing on cloud platform engineering, DevSecOps, and AI workload security."
>
  <section class="container-page py-20">
    <p class="eyebrow mb-4">Writing</p>
    <h1 class="title-display mb-6 hero-gradient max-w-3xl leading-tight">
      Notes from the field.
    </h1>
    <p class="body-muted max-w-2xl text-lg">
      Short technical posts on the work I do — cloud platform engineering,
      DevSecOps, Terraform patterns, and the edges of securing AI
      workloads. First posts landing soon.
    </p>

    <div class="mt-12 card p-8">
      <p class="title-card mb-2">No posts yet.</p>
      <p class="body-muted text-sm">
        First in the queue: a deep dive on
        <span class="code-inline">harvtech.co.uk</span>'s architecture —
        why Standard SKU Front Door, what the Trivy
        <span class="code-inline">AZU-0012</span> finding really means
        when you can't satisfy it on your chosen tier, and how to
        document those trade-offs honestly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
